  "id": "Compound::DB00259 - Gene::771",
  "verbalization": "Sulfanilamide appears to interact with Ca12 through a series of biochemical pathways, as evidenced by its binding to Ca6 and Ca9, which in turn participate in the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide and carbonate dehydratase activity, both of which are associated with Ca12. These interactions suggest a potential role for Sulfanilamide in modulating the activity of Ca12 through indirect mechanisms involving carbon dioxide and phosphate metabolism. The consistent involvement of Ca12 in these processes, coupled with the high scores from the three paths, indicates a plausible link between Sulfanilamide and Ca12, likely mediated through the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide. The mechanisms appear to be interconnected, with Ca12 acting as a downstream participant in multiple metabolic pathways, reinforcing the hypothesis that Sulfanilamide may influence Ca12 through these indirect pathways.",
